  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "PERCENTILE.EXC rejects k <= 1/(n+1) or k >= n/(n+1) with #NUM!, while .INC/.EXC return #NAME? in compat-1",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, PERCENTILE and PERCENTILE.INC interpolate linearly at rank 1 + k*(n - 1) over [0, 1], whereas PERCENTILE.EXC interpolates at rank k*(n + 1) and returns #NUM! whenever rank < 1 or rank > n (for example outside (1/(n+1), n/(n+1))). Under compatibility version 1, @PERCENTILE.INC and @PERCENTILE.EXC evaluate to #NAME? while PERCENTILE remains unprefixed.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (rows 173-175), and matched across 2,851/2,851 PERCENTILE, 2,849/2,849 PERCENTILE.EXC, and 2,855/2,855 PERCENTILE.INC full-bank rows.",
